cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MAVRIC: Multimodal Audio-Video-RFID Interaction and Control"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 0.9.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/JesusJBallesteros/MAVRIC"
url: "https://github.com/JesusJBallesteros/MAVRIC"
authors:
  - given-names: "Jesus J."
    family-names: "Ballesteros"
    affiliation: "Neural Basis of Learning Lab, Institute of Cognitive Neuroscience (IKN), Ruhr-Universität Bochum"
abstract: >-
  A behavioural suite for experiments with RFID-tagged subjects: synchronized video, audio and RFID
  identification, with event-driven outputs for task control and interaction. Records RFID reads, one or more
  cameras and microphones on one clock, checks the synchronization with a random sync pulse, provides blind
  ground-truth labeling of place occupancy and sound events, compares RFID with the labels, drives
  event-triggered outputs and video clips, and prepares video for DeepLabCut.
keywords:
  - RFID
  - animal behaviour
  - video
  - audio
  - synchronization
  - task control
references:
  - type: software
    title: "MultiRFID: multi-backend RFID logging for animal behaviour experiments"
    authors:
      - given-names: "Jesus J."
        family-names: "Ballesteros"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/JesusJBallesteros/MultiRFID"
